    slug: "camping-fees-australia-2026", title: "Camping Fees Australia 2026: National Park Prices by State", description: "National park camping in 2026: $7.75 a person in Queensland, $10 to $20 an adult in WA and the NT, from $16 a site in Victoria, plus entry fees.", category: "Costs & budget", region: "Australia", readTime: 5,
    places: ["Parks Victoria","Ikara-Flinders Ranges","Karijini","Mount Field","Holiday parks"], imageAlt: "Caravan and tent at an Australian campground", intro: "Australian national park camping in 2026 runs from free to more than $40 a night at the busiest serviced sites, such as Tidal River at Wilsons Promontory: Queensland charges $7.75 per person, Western Australia and the Northern Territory $10 to $20 per adult, Victoria's half-price bookable campgrounds start at $16 a site, and some NSW campgrounds charge nothing beyond a $6 booking fee. Park entry, passes and whether the fee is per person or per site change the total more than the headline rate.",
